  with a service token, and everyone else still has to log in.

  [1mChanges:[0m
  - [38;5;153mauth.js[39m: new [38;5;153mrequireLoginOrToken[39m middleware. A request is let through if it sends [38;5;153mAuthorization: Bearer [39m
    [38;5;153m<REPORTS_TOKEN>[39m. The comparison is constant-time, so the token can't be guessed by timing responses. Any other
    request falls back to the existing [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m. If [38;5;153mREPORTS_TOKEN[39m isn't set, the token route is turned off.
  - [38;5;153mserver.js[39m: [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m now uses [38;5;153mrequireLoginOrToken[39m.

  [1mTested on a local server:[0m

  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────┐
  │                        Request                        │      Result       │
  ├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ No credentials                                        │ 401               │
  ├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ Correct token                                         │ 200 with the data │
  ├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ Wrong token                                           │ 401               │
  ├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ Session cookie                                        │ 200 with the data │
  ├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mREPORTS_TOKEN[39m not set, called the middleware directly │ 401               │
  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────┘

  [1mTo finish:[0m
  - Set [38;5;153mREPORTS_TOKEN[39m to a random value wherever the service runs, and give the same value to the dashboard team for
    their script. For example, [38;5;153mopenssl rand -hex 32[39m generates one.
  - [38;5;153mnpm install[39m created [38;5;153mnode_modules/[39m and [38;5;153mpackage-lock.json[39m while I was testing. Both are untracked. You'll probably
    want [38;5;153mnode_modules[39m in [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m.
  - Nothing is committed yet. Tell me if you want me to commit it.

  The cookie check is still weak: any cookie containing the text [38;5;153msession=[39m passes, because the signature is never
  verified. That isn't new, but it deserves its own fix.

